# ⛔ 6.7.14 — A REDECLARATION WHOSE INITIALIZER FOLDS (`= 2 + 1`, `= -5`, `= (7)`) IS COMPARED as a literal one is
# (CHKDUPVAL: "redefined with conflicting value", a same value silent). Only the exact `= NUM ;` was, so `var a = 5;
# var a = 2 + 1;` compiled silently while the prior side compared any folded constant
# (issues/archived/2026-10-15-redeclared-global-folded-later-value-not-compared.md). Not over an enum constant (CHK_ENUM_SHADOW's
# hard error is the one report there) nor a top-level const (refused at the name), and `chk_has` stays 0: it also gates
# CHK_ENUM_SHADOW. `has` / `v` = the declaration's fold. CHANGELOG [6.7.14]
fn _gv_dup_folded(S, noff, has, v, is_struct): i64 {
    if (has == 0) { return 0; }
    if (is_struct != 0) { return 0; }
